📦 1. Array - Find Maximum Element
➔ Solution (Java):
java
Copy
Edit
int[] arr = {2, 7, 3, 9, 5};
int max = arr[0];
for (int i = 1; i < arr.length; i++) {
    if (arr[i] > max) {
        max = arr[i];
    }
}
System.out.println("Maximum Element: " + max);
➔ Dry Run:
Initial max = 2

Compare with 7 → max = 7

Compare with 3 → no change

Compare with 9 → max = 9

Compare with 5 → no change

Final Max = 9

➔ Time Complexity:
O(n) → One pass through array.

➔ Space Complexity:
O(1) → Only a variable for max.

📄 2. String - Check Palindrome
➔ Solution (Java):
java
Copy
Edit
String s = "racecar";
boolean isPalindrome = true;
int start = 0, end = s.length() - 1;
while (start < end) {
    if (s.charAt(start) != s.charAt(end)) {
        isPalindrome = false;
        break;
    }
    start++;
    end--;
}
System.out.println("Is Palindrome: " + isPalindrome);
➔ Dry Run:
'r' == 'r' ✅

'a' == 'a' ✅

'c' == 'c' ✅

Center reached → Palindrome ✅

➔ Time Complexity:
O(n) → Traverses only half of the string.

➔ Space Complexity:
O(1) → Only few variables.

🔗 3. Singly Linked List - Print All Elements
➔ Solution (Java):
java
Copy
Edit
class Node {
    int data;
    Node next;
    Node(int data) {
        this.data = data;
        this.next = null;
    }
}

Node head = new Node(10);
head.next = new Node(20);
head.next.next = new Node(30);

// Traversal
Node temp = head;
while (temp != null) {
    System.out.print(temp.data + " ");
    temp = temp.next;
}
➔ Dry Run:
Print 10

Move to next → Print 20

Move to next → Print 30

Output: 10 20 30

➔ Time Complexity:
O(n) → Traverse each node once.

➔ Space Complexity:
O(1) → No extra space, just a temp pointer.

🔗🔙 4. Doubly Linked List - Print in Reverse
➔ Solution (Java):
java

class Node {
    int data;
    Node next, prev;
    Node(int data) {
        this.data = data;
        this.next = this.prev = null;
    }
}

Node head = new Node(10);
Node second = new Node(20);
Node third = new Node(30);
head.next = second;
second.prev = head;
second.next = third;
third.prev = second;

// Move to last node
Node temp = head;
while (temp.next != null) {
    temp = temp.next;
}

// Traverse backward
while (temp != null) {
    System.out.print(temp.data + " ");
    temp = temp.prev;
}
➔ Dry Run:
Move to 30

Print 30

Move to 20 → Print 20

Move to 10 → Print 10

Output: 30 20 10

➔ Time Complexity:
O(n) → Traverse each node once.

➔ Space Complexity:
O(1) → No extra space.

🥞 5. Stack - Print Top Element
➔ Solution (Java):
java

import java.util.Stack;
Stack<Integer> stack = new Stack<>();
stack.push(5);
stack.push(10);
stack.push(15);
System.out.println("Top Element: " + stack.peek());
➔ Dry Run:
Push 5

Push 10

Push 15

Peek → 15

Output: Top Element: 15

➔ Time Complexity:
O(1) → Push, pop, peek operations in Stack are O(1).

➔ Space Complexity:
O(n) → Stack holds all elements.

